# 22. Required Accounting Invariants

Implement automated tests for these invariants.

### Energy issuance invariant

Total issued energy credits must not exceed total verified eligible energy, accounting for any explicitly documented adjustments.

### Allocation invariant

Allocated energy must not exceed eligible community energy available for allocation.

### Consumer compensation invariant

Compensated consumption must not exceed eligible verified consumption.

### Retirement invariant

Each credit retirement must correspond to an authorized burn and must not be processed twice.

### Supply invariant

Token supply must reconcile with confirmed minting and burning events, subject to any other explicitly authorized supply-changing operations.

### Trade invariant

Settled trade quantities must not exceed the quantity authorized and available for settlement.

### Financial invariant

A monetary obligation must not be marked paid without corresponding confirmed payment evidence or an explicitly labeled simulated-ledger transaction.

### Auditability invariant

Every confirmed credit issuance, trade, compensation, retirement, and settlement must be traceable to its source records.

